<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><a href="https://www.relay.fm/focused/266">On this episode of <em>Focused</em></a>, Mike and I look at how AI becomes a distraction precisely because it feels like work. We cover tool tourism, infinite collaboration, system procrastination, cognitive debt, and authority drift, then set a few boundaries that keep the robot useful without surrendering your focus.</p>
